He'd only swat down their planes.

247
00:14:13,060 --> 00:14:15,050
Perhaps you could...

248
00:14:15,228 --> 00:14:16,456
...lie.

249
00:14:17,597 --> 00:14:19,155
Well, I'm not above that.

250
00:14:19,332 --> 00:14:21,391
- Bull?
- I can't hear you.

251
00:14:21,568 --> 00:14:22,899
No, don't lean over! No! No!

252
00:14:23,069 --> 00:14:24,593
Bull!

253
00:14:25,372 --> 00:14:27,431
We need your help.

254
00:14:30,110 --> 00:14:33,739
Liz fell down and broke her leg,
and we can't move her.

255
00:14:33,914 --> 00:14:35,313
- What?
- That stinks.

256
00:14:35,482 --> 00:14:38,279
Would you help, Bull?
She's in a lot of pain.

257
00:14:38,450 --> 00:14:40,680
- Moan. Moan.
- No. It's silly.

258
00:14:40,853 --> 00:14:42,548
So is a contempt charge.

259
00:14:45,558 --> 00:14:47,958
Will you help us, Bull?
It's pretty bad.

260
00:14:50,362 --> 00:14:52,296
Bull, what do you say?

261
00:14:52,631 --> 00:14:55,361
- Okay. I'll be right down.
- Great. Great.

262
00:14:55,534 --> 00:14:58,298
No, no, no, no, no!
Take the long way.

263
00:15:05,343 --> 00:15:07,538
This doesn't smell like outside.

264
00:15:07,712 --> 00:15:10,010
- You again?
- The judge, right?

265
00:15:10,181 --> 00:15:13,514
- That's right.
- What is this place, a maze?

266
00:15:14,018 --> 00:15:15,679
I'll call security.

267
00:15:15,853 --> 00:15:20,085
Why can't they make those
"you are here" maps in Braille?

268
00:15:20,925 --> 00:15:22,358
Here you go, Mr. Foley.

269
00:15:22,527 --> 00:15:25,461
Why don't you just have a seat
right over here.

270
00:15:26,496 --> 00:15:29,556
- Bull.
- Yeah, okay. Where's?

271
00:15:30,767 --> 00:15:32,826
What's going on?
You don't look hurt to me.

272
00:15:34,237 --> 00:15:36,000
He lied.

273
00:15:36,907 --> 00:15:39,000
- I get it.
- Bull, I had to talk to you.

274
00:15:39,176 --> 00:15:42,202
Don't waste your breath.
It won't affect my decision.

275
00:15:42,379 --> 00:15:44,006
What decision?

276
00:15:46,183 --> 00:15:47,912
I've decided I'm gonna go away...

277
00:15:48,085 --> 00:15:51,611
...and not associate with any other
human beings as long as I live.

278
00:15:52,388 --> 00:15:55,585
Boy! Now that's what I call a decision.

279
00:15:55,758 --> 00:15:58,488
- Bull, you can't do that.
- Who's gonna stop me?

280
00:15:58,661 --> 00:16:00,822
Where would you go?
I mean, what would you do?

281
00:16:01,831 --> 00:16:03,059
Canada, maybe.

282
00:16:03,232 --> 00:16:04,790
I could be a lumberjack.

283
00:16:04,967 --> 00:16:08,266
Or I could go up to the North Pole,
one of those radar tracking stations.

284
00:16:08,604 --> 00:16:10,765
I don't care! People won't have to
deal with me.

285
00:16:10,940 --> 00:16:13,874
I won't have to deal with them,
which as far as I'm concerned...

286
00:16:14,042 --> 00:16:15,532
...is good riddance.

287
00:16:15,710 --> 00:16:17,644
Amen.

288
00:16:19,080 --> 00:16:20,604
Who are you?

289
00:16:21,282 --> 00:16:23,842
My name is Foley. Ralph Foley.

290
00:16:24,285 --> 00:16:25,775
Shut up, Ralph.

291
00:16:26,855 --> 00:16:28,117
Right.

292
00:16:28,490 --> 00:16:30,253
- I'm going. See you.
- So that's it.

293
00:16:30,425 --> 00:16:33,724
You're just gonna walk out
after we've worked together all these...

294
00:16:34,429 --> 00:16:36,124
...weeks?

295
00:16:36,297 --> 00:16:39,197
- Bull, we want you to stay.
- Yeah, that's right.

296
00:16:39,366 --> 00:16:41,231
We all do.

297
00:16:41,769 --> 00:16:43,202
Dan?

298
00:16:43,570 --> 00:16:45,561
I'll take a taco.

299
00:16:48,142 --> 00:16:49,370
I'm getting out of here!

300
00:16:49,543 --> 00:16:52,842
Okay. If that's the way you feel,
go ahead!

301
00:16:53,947 --> 00:16:55,175
Oh, come on. I was kidding.

302
00:16:55,349 --> 00:16:56,680
Bull.

303
00:16:56,850 --> 00:16:59,080
Bull, maybe this is
none of my business...

304
00:16:59,253 --> 00:17:02,619
...but frankly, I feel like you're acting
like a little child here.

305
00:17:02,789 --> 00:17:04,723
You're running away
from your problems...

306
00:17:04,891 --> 00:17:06,916
...instead of facing them like a man.

307
00:17:07,393 --> 00:17:10,556
This is my problem.
How can I run away from that?

308
00:17:10,730 --> 00:17:13,631
Boy, there's one thing I really hate,
it's self-pity.

309
00:17:14,233 --> 00:17:16,531
Hey, before you go away, pal...

310
00:17:16,803 --> 00:17:19,738
...I wanna, I wanna shake your hand.

311
00:17:22,475 --> 00:17:23,703
There.

312
00:17:24,042 --> 00:17:25,771
I never thought I'd meet the man...

313
00:17:25,944 --> 00:17:29,402
...who felt that his problem
was worse than mine.

314
00:17:29,848 --> 00:17:31,782
Why? What's your problem?

315
00:17:33,018 --> 00:17:34,986
I'm blind, man.

316
00:17:36,655 --> 00:17:37,952
Yeah, see?

317
00:17:38,123 --> 00:17:40,591
Dark glasses and a cane.

318
00:17:40,792 --> 00:17:43,886
I thought you were just being
fashionable.

319
00:17:44,796 --> 00:17:48,424
I'm afraid Bull doesn't pay much attention
to outward appearances, Mr. Foley.

320
00:17:48,599 --> 00:17:50,362
No? Well, me neither.

321
00:17:50,534 --> 00:17:52,559
But most people do.

322
00:17:52,737 --> 00:17:54,671
I get hauled in for shoplifting,
they say:

323
00:17:54,839 --> 00:17:58,605
"Oh, look at him.
Let the poor blind man go."

324
00:17:58,776 --> 00:18:00,539
But in a way, it works for me.

325
00:18:00,711 --> 00:18:05,478
- I had 15 busts, only four convictions.
- Actually, I think it's 19 arrests.

326
00:18:05,649 --> 00:18:06,877
Is that his arrest jacket?

327
00:18:07,051 --> 00:18:08,643
- Yeah.
- Let me see it.

328
00:18:09,153 --> 00:18:10,381
Goodbye.

329
00:18:10,554 --> 00:18:12,384
Boy, Bull sure had this guy pegged.

330
00:18:12,789 --> 00:18:14,586
- What?
- Yeah, the evidence is all here.

331
00:18:14,758 --> 00:18:16,749
You're certainly guilty, Mr. Foley.

332
00:18:16,926 --> 00:18:19,952
- Maybe, but who's gonna send me up?
- I am.

333
00:18:20,130 --> 00:18:21,791
- Yeah, sure.
- I'm not kidding.

334
00:18:21,965 --> 00:18:23,762
That blind stuff didn't work on Bull...

335
00:18:23,933 --> 00:18:26,766
...it doesn't work on me either, right, Bull?
- Yeah, I guess.

336
00:18:26,936 --> 00:18:29,427
You wanna be treated like a criminal,
Mr. Foley?

337
00:18:29,606 --> 00:18:32,166
I'm gonna send you up for 14 months.

338
00:18:32,609 --> 00:18:34,236
That's a little rough, isn't it?

339
00:18:34,410 --> 00:18:37,867
- Hey, life is rough, isn't it, Bull?
- Yeah.

340
00:18:38,046 --> 00:18:40,606
- You're right, Bull. This guy is scum.
- I didn't say...

341
00:18:40,783 --> 00:18:44,219
I mean, some other judge might give him
probation because he's blind.

342
00:18:44,386 --> 00:18:47,549
You know, take pity. But Bull doesn't have
any pity for him, do you?

343
00:18:48,357 --> 00:18:49,984
- Well...
- And I don't either. No.

344
00:18:50,159 --> 00:18:53,856
What am I supposed to do, treat him nice?
I mean, remand him into the custody...

345
00:18:54,029 --> 00:18:56,293
...of some responsible person?

346
00:18:56,465 --> 00:19:00,195
Come on. What responsible person
would wanna help out...

347
00:19:00,368 --> 00:19:06,705
...a miserable, rotten, sneaky little
lowlife of a criminal like him?

348
00:19:14,849 --> 00:19:16,783
Can I have him?

349
00:19:18,085 --> 00:19:19,416
What?

350
00:19:19,587 --> 00:19:23,147
If you could see your way clear
to releasing him, Your Honor...

351
00:19:23,323 --> 00:19:26,656
...l'd accept the responsibility for him.

352
00:19:26,827 --> 00:19:29,352
Hey, what the hell is going on
around here?

353
00:19:29,796 --> 00:19:31,354
I don't know, Mr. Foley.

354
00:19:34,034 --> 00:19:35,467
Listen...

355
00:19:35,635 --> 00:19:37,262
...I just wanna help.

356
00:19:37,437 --> 00:19:38,665
You mind?

357
00:19:40,073 --> 00:19:41,802
Why do you wanna help?

358
00:19:44,878 --> 00:19:47,072
It makes me feel good.

359
00:19:48,147 --> 00:19:50,638
I don't get a chance all that often...

360
00:19:51,750 --> 00:19:53,149
...and I miss it.

361
00:19:54,453 --> 00:19:56,648
I guess I know what you mean.

362
00:19:57,223 --> 00:19:59,157
I used to help people too.

363
00:19:59,325 --> 00:20:02,920
But they don't ask me
quite as often anymore.

364
00:20:06,298 --> 00:20:08,061
I'm asking.

365
00:20:10,369 --> 00:20:11,596
Yeah.

366
00:20:11,769 --> 00:20:13,532
I guess you are.

367
00:20:15,340 --> 00:20:18,366
Come on, judge.
Give the kid a break.

368
00:20:19,210 --> 00:20:20,837
Let him have me.

369
00:20:21,012 --> 00:20:22,411
- Oh, I don't know.
- Come on!

370
00:20:24,315 --> 00:20:25,907
What about the North Pole?

371
00:20:26,084 --> 00:20:28,177
I still got my two weeks' vacation.

372
00:20:28,953 --> 00:20:33,390
Well, okay, but I'd feel better
if you were in a responsible position.

373
00:20:35,959 --> 00:20:38,894
- Is it official?
- As of this moment, you're back on the job.

374
00:20:39,062 --> 00:20:40,290
Great.

375
00:20:40,464 --> 00:20:42,056
Can I go to lunch?

376
00:20:44,768 --> 00:20:46,360
Come on, Ralph. I'll take you home.

377
00:20:46,536 --> 00:20:48,697
Okay, Bull.

378
00:20:52,175 --> 00:20:54,439
That stuff with me and Ralph...

379
00:20:55,245 --> 00:20:57,304
...I know what you did.

380
00:20:57,581 --> 00:20:59,309
It's my hobby.

381
00:20:59,982 --> 00:21:03,975
Oh, yeah?
Hey, mine is stamp collecting.

382
00:21:06,923 --> 00:21:09,756
Really? I'd like to see
your collection sometime.

383
00:21:09,926 --> 00:21:11,553
So would I.

384
00:21:15,031 --> 00:21:16,658
Watch your head.

385
00:21:23,371 --> 00:21:25,339
<i>Not bad, amigo.</i>

386
00:21:25,507 --> 00:21:27,407
<i>Gracias.</i>

387
00:21:28,143 --> 00:21:30,611
I'm starting to catch on to you,
you know.

388
00:21:30,779 --> 00:21:34,681
I saw those little wheels spinning
in your head.

389
00:21:34,849 --> 00:21:37,113
I knew that you had some kind of plan...

390
00:21:37,285 --> 00:21:43,520
...to bring those two people together
like a human jigsaw puzzle, without ever...

391
00:21:45,859 --> 00:21:47,656
We'll talk later.

392
00:21:55,769 --> 00:21:57,566
So?

393
00:21:57,738 --> 00:21:59,228
What do you think?

394
00:22:04,845 --> 00:22:06,870
Let's have a cigarette.

395
00:22:16,155 --> 00:22:17,520
Hello.

396
00:22:19,492 --> 00:22:21,483
I thought you quit.

397
00:22:28,067 --> 00:22:29,432
I'm back.

398
00:22:30,937 --> 00:22:32,871
I can see that.

399
00:22:33,272 --> 00:22:35,671
You know, I was worried about you.

400
00:22:35,841 --> 00:22:37,138
I'm sorry.

401
00:22:37,309 --> 00:22:38,640
You're sorry?

402
00:22:38,810 --> 00:22:40,835
Let me tell you something.

403
00:22:41,013 --> 00:22:42,844
Don't you ever...

404
00:22:43,015 --> 00:22:47,975
...pull any stunt like that again
while I'm around here.

405
00:22:48,153 --> 00:22:54,058
And don't you ever walk out
and leave me alone on the job.

406
00:22:54,226 --> 00:22:59,595
And don't you ever forget
that I have the seniority here...

407
00:22:59,764 --> 00:23:03,530
...and what I say goes.

408
00:23:04,535 --> 00:23:06,298
Yes, ma'am.

409
00:23:07,671 --> 00:23:10,970
- How about a beer at Muldoon's?
- Sure.

410
00:23:11,142 --> 00:23:13,770
It's your turn to buy.

